From: fil-c-utils maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Use sched_yield under Fil-C on AArch64

Fil-C traps when curl's global-init lock executes the inline AArch64 yield
instruction. Skip that optional assembly under Fil-C so the existing
HAVE_SCHED_YIELD fallback handles the spin wait instead.

--- a/lib/easy_lock.h
+++ b/lib/easy_lock.h
@@ -68,7 +68,7 @@ static CURL_INLINE void curl_simple_lock_lock(curl_simple_lock *lock)
       /* Reduce load (not mandatory) */
 #ifdef HAVE_BUILTIN_IA32_PAUSE
       __builtin_ia32_pause();
-#elif defined(__aarch64__)
+#elif defined(__aarch64__) && !defined(__FILC__)
       __asm__ volatile("yield" ::: "memory");
 #elif defined(HAVE_SCHED_YIELD)
       sched_yield();
